              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "praestō, praestāre — \"to make good, to fulfil; to excel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fidem praestitit. He kept his word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "praestō, praestāre, praestitī, praestitum. Fidem praestāre, to make one's word good; with the dative, to stand out above: omnibus praestat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "praestō is built from prae \"before, in front\" and stō \"to stand\" (Lewis & Short): to stand out in front, then to stand good for a promise."
            }
          ]
        },
